  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows 10
      or 11, wait for "CLICK" (~5 seconds while the shaders
      compile and the soundtrack renders), then click to go
      fullscreen. No server, no browser flags. ESC exits
      fullscreen. A discrete GPU is expected. Tested on Edge
      with an RTX 5090 (0.9-2.2 ms/frame at 1080p).

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    inside
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      One raymarched scene shader switches cleanly across six
      acts centered on a faceted 4-pointed Gemini star SDF
      that stays camera-facing via analytic yaw alignment.
      To keep ANGLE/D3D11 compilation fast (~3-5 s instead of
      32 s), map() has zero inner loops and only two call
      sites (primary march + Z-bounded tetrahedron normal),
      and all volumetric neon glows, Swarm laser message-board
      filaments and travelling data packets are computed in
      closed form via ray-to-segment distance (zero grain).

      The post shader combines a 12-tap Vogel-disc bokeh DoF,
      5-octave mipmap bloom, ACES filmic tone mapping, Swiss
      HUD overlays, and a live anti-aliased Zopfli byte
      countdown sampled directly from a shared 2D canvas font
      atlas (digits 0-9 packed alongside the title on row 0).

      The soundtrack is rendered on the GPU at 48 kHz into a
      4096x1550 RGBA32F texture (132.27 s). Eight evolving
      F#m9/Lydian chords feed zero-click crossfaded FM glass
      pads, 4-note overlapping inharmonic glass celesta arps,
      an original orbital/breakbeat percussion groove with
      metallic FM hats, ghost snares and 8-bar fills, a true-
      sub + resonant 4th-order acid bass with turnarounds, a
      64-step sustained melody with diatonic 3rd counter-
      harmony and 3-tap dotted-8th ping-pong echo, and a
      zero-aliasing integrated Shepard Zopfli crush — split
      into dry (RG) and a 4-line Householder FDN hall reverb
      (BA) in JavaScript.

